  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - pysm has no model=self dynamic-injection mechanism; it requires explicit 
StateMachine subclasses/instances with State/Transition/Event objects, so 
self.state and self.start_fill()/self.level_reached() etc. cannot be 
auto-generated without restructuring the class.
    - pysm does not support the 'conditions' and 'after' string-based callback 
resolution used by transitions.add_transition; guard and action callbacks would
need to be re-wired using pysm's State.handlers/Transition action mechanism, 
which is a structurally different callback model.
    - The wildcard source state '*' used in trip() (transitions-specific) has 
no direct pysm equivalent; pysm transitions require explicit source states, so 
all states would need enumerated FAULT transitions, changing the machine's 
transition table semantics.
    - This is a structural rewrite of TankController's FSM wiring and callback 
dispatch model, not a drop-in import swap — matches the stated pitfalls 
indicating the migration exceeds simple glue-code wrapping in critical parts 
(state model + dispatch), even though a wrapper can approximate some of the 
surface API.

