└── email/notification sending backend
    ├── Candidates : smtplib, apprise
    ├── Used APIs  : SMTP, sendmail
    ├── Pitfalls   : smtplib.sendmail() takes explicit envelope 
    │   sender/recipients and a raw RFC822 message string, while apprise uses a
    │   notify(title, body) call against pre-configured service URLs — requires
    │   building an apprise Apprise() object and registering an SMTP-style URL;
    │   apprise abstracts away raw message construction (From/To/Subject 
    │   headers), so the EmailNotifier.notify() method's manual message 
    │   formatting would need to be replaced with apprise's title/body 
    │   parameters; Return value semantics differ: smtplib.sendmail returns a 
    │   dict of failed recipients; apprise.notify returns a boolean 
    │   success/failure; Dependency injection of the 'smtp' object assumes an 
    │   object with a sendmail() method — swapping to apprise requires the 
    │   injected object to instead be an Apprise instance with notify(), 
    │   breaking the current constructor's implicit interface contract
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file's docstring explicitly identifies apprise as the intended 
        substitution target for smtplib-based email notification. Both can be 
        used to deliver alarm notifications to operators, with apprise 
        supporting SMTP among many other transports, making it a plausible 
        drop-in for the notification role even though the underlying API 
        differs substantially.

